# Everything checks out LF, on every platform.
#
# Two of the formatters here treat a CRLF file as entirely unformatted and
# rewrite the whole thing: gofmt, and Prettier, whose endOfLine defaults to lf.
# Left to core.autocrlf - true by default on Windows, the CI runner included - a
# checkout hands both of them CRLF and every file is reported.
#
# That is not hypothetical. This started as `*.go text eol=lf` alone, to stop
# `gofmt -l` flagging the whole tree; the frontend never got the same treatment,
# and the first `prettier --check` to run on a Windows runner failed with every
# file in frontend/ listed, `.prettierrc` among them. Same cause, same fix,
# applied once rather than per language.
#
# text=auto still lets git detect binary content and leave it alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
